TEXT 600 40 Left 2 ;LE-53 lock driver (low-side NMOS switch)
TEXT 600 72 Left 2 ;Rcoil + Lcoil = LE-53 coil (5V / 2W -> 12.5 ohm, L is an assumption)
TEXT 600 104 Left 2 ;D1 = flyback diode across the coil
TEXT 600 136 Left 2 ;Rpd keeps the lock closed while GPIO is floating (boot)
TEXT 600 168 Left 2 ;V1 is a separate 5V supply. Connect its GND to Raspberry Pi GND
TEXT 600 232 Left 2 !.tran 0 30m 0 1u
TEXT 600 264 Left 2 !.model NMOS_LL VDMOS(Vto=1.2 Kp=8 Rd=20m Rs=10m Rg=2 Cgdmax=150p Cgdmin=15p Cgs=250p Cjo=80p Is=1e-12 Rb=20m)
TEXT 600 296 Left 2 !.model D_FLY D(Is=31.7u Rs=51m N=1.373 Cjo=110p M=0.35 Eg=0.69 Xti=2)
TEXT 600 336 Left 2 ;NMOS_LL / D_FLY are generic models for simulation.
TEXT 600 360 Left 2 ;Real parts: logic-level NMOS fully on at Vgs=2.5V (e.g. IRLML6344), Schottky 1A (e.g. 1N5819)
